1
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,060
And just try getting away from me.

2
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:24,240
Anyone who's broke, come to me.

3
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:28,940
I'm broke too, but don't worry about it.

4
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:32,760
Look at the blue sky.

5
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,980
White clouds.

6
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:09,380
You're best friends with Noriko Fushihara,
the one Reiko modeled for?

7
00:01:10,260 --> 00:01:10,980
Really?

8
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:11,814
Yeah,

9
00:01:11,864 --> 00:01:15,540
She seems to come over to
Reiko's apartment a lot.

10
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:17,480
What?

11
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,540
Because if the senior officer finds out,
he'll pester me to introduce him.

12
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:23,460
I was keeping it a secret.

13
00:01:23,980 --> 00:01:24,858
Damn it,

14
00:01:24,908 --> 00:01:28,620
Reiko's so lucky, honestly.

15
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:32,720
If I could switch places with anyone,
I'd love to switch with Reiko.

16
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:36,200
Hello hello, everybody!

17
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:38,500
This voice is...

18
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:41,720
Everyone at the police box,
long time no see.

19
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,220
I feel like you've been
coming by quite often, though.

20
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:47,540
Along with some strange inventions, yeah.

21
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:51,100
So what on earth are you here for today?

22
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:53,440
Good question, Gorilla-kun.

23
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:57,620
Today I've brought the greatest
invention of this century.

24
00:01:58,340 --> 00:01:59,340
Just as I thought.

25
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:01,940
And this is the invention.

26
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:09,220
Yes, Gorilla-ken! This is humanity's shining hope, the Nobel Shamer.
It's not a dream, it's a once-in-a-lifetime, one-of-a-kind great invention.

27
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:11,880
Eeeeeeh!

28
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:19,520
Isn't this a purikura machine?
No, it's not, I hear.

29
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:29,360
Then what is it? This is a transformation machine that
lets you swap appearances with the person you want to be.

30
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:32,140
Transformation machine.

31
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:35,100
This is the transformation machine.

32
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:38,740
No matter how you look at it,
it's nothing but a purikura machine.

33
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:41,600
That's where amateurs go wrong.

34
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:43,480
Get off at the station,
then it's a five-minute walk.

35
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:48,380
This is a truly remarkable invention.

36
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,140
Something seems fishy.

37
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:53,560
Didn't you bring something similar before?

38
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:55,660
So, Gorilla-kun.

39
00:02:56,060 --> 00:02:58,900
I'll let you be the
first to use this machine.

40
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:09,620
Good, right? It's a chance to be the first
person ever to use this historic great invention.

41
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:16,640
No way! What's lucky about it? Basically you're making me your guinea pig,
aren't you?

42
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:20,820
I'm not giving my strong body
to your experiment, got it?

43
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:24,720
Don't say such a cold thing, Gorilla-kun.

44
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:26,460
Please.

45
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:29,940
Anyway,
if you're swapping places with someone,

46
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:32,560
you can't run an experiment alone, can you?

47
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:37,340
So, I'd like Nakagawa-kun
to cooperate with us too.

48
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:40,420
I don't want to either, you know.

49
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:43,260
No way, absolutely not.

50
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:44,780
Absolutely not, no matter what.

51
00:03:44,780 --> 00:03:46,580
No, no way, definitely not.

52
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:48,760
Absolutely, positively not.

53
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:51,380
No matter how much you beg, no, no, no.

54
00:03:51,380 --> 00:03:54,280
No matter how much you ask,
it's a big no, no, no.

55
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:57,540
Look at this.

56
00:03:57,900 --> 00:04:00,980
What's this? A new photo sticker!

57
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:04,000
Ryo-chan, let's take one together!

58
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,960
Reiko, it's not what you think!

59
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:15,720
Senpai

60
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:18,240
I'm over here.

61
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:19,900
W-well then.

62
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:23,120
Looks like the experiment
was a complete failure.

63
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:24,120
What?

64
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,940
That can't be right.

65
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:29,700
But nothing bad happened,
so that's good, isn't it?

66
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:32,440
Huh? What are you talking about?

67
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:34,820
Nothing, nothing.

68
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:35,940
That's strange.

69
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:39,380
I'm Reiko, so

70
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:40,780
and I'm Ryo-chan.

71
00:04:54,020 --> 00:05:23,920


72
00:05:57,900 --> 00:06:03,000
Who's that? You're a suspicious character!
Protect the young lady!

73
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:03,460
Mm.

74
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:37,840
You're Shūkichi Hirayama, right?

75
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:45,360
This is the piece I played
at Father's birthday.

76
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:48,240
Indeed,
this is a piece the young lady is good at.

77
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:51,220
But anyone can play it
if they just practice.

78
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:00,820
Yes, Reiko's special fruit cake.

79
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:08,120
Delicious!
It's exactly the young lady's taste!

80
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:11,060
See! This recipe is a
closely guarded secret!

81
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,920
You! How did you get this?

82
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:14,440
Maybe you stole the recipe!

83
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:24,720
Well? Hirayama!

84
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:26,660
What do you want me to say?

85
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:29,340
You must have watched my dancing often!

86
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:32,380
You've always had me drive
you to and from ballet!

87
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:34,460
How do you know that?

88
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:37,980
Your granddaughter's name is Aya-chan.

89
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:40,600
She's in fifth grade this year, isn't she?

90
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:43,020
We went to celebrate
Aya-chan's entrance to school

91
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:45,400
with the pink randoseru
Dad gave her as a present.

92
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:47,240
I picked that one out myself.

93
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:51,860
Only Pyunpyun Maru-sama
and Lady Reikō know that.

94
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:55,220
So you really are Lady Reikō?

95
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:57,200
Yes, it's me, Reiko.

96
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:59,220
Why did you end up looking like that?

97
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:01,360
I don't know either.

98
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:04,520
I woke up this morning and I was like this.

99
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:06,840
Hirayama.

100
00:08:08,620 --> 00:08:10,280
I'm done with this, I don't care anymore.

101
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:11,140
Lady Kocho.

102
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:12,600
I see.

103
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:14,780
Esaki's photo sticker came up just now,

104
00:08:14,780 --> 00:08:16,280
so that's why she came asking about it

105
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:18,420
But still,

106
00:08:18,420 --> 00:08:19,660
what great legs.

107
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:21,960
They're more than half her body!

108
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:24,580
And she's pretty tall, too.

109
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:25,940
Well, for now,

110
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:27,460
let's go check out the police box.

111
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:29,880
Senpai.

112
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:32,200
I made some clam miso soup, want to try it?

113
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:37,980
Seriously.

114
00:08:37,980 --> 00:08:39,380
Hey, hey, Reiko-san.

115
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:57,780
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

116
00:08:57,780 --> 00:08:59,720
I only borrowed it, that's all.

117
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:01,880
"Only borrowed it"? How could you say that?

118
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:04,400
There it is! There it is! There it is!

119
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:07,100
So that means Reiko-san
and senpai are maybe...

120
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:10,320
Could they be in that kind of relationship?

121
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:13,180
We've finally been found out.

122
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:20,440
I can't believe Reiko-san
would do something like this.

123
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:25,180
Is it so wrong for me
and Reiko to be dating?

124
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:27,180
I feel sick, you know.

125
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:30,680
Hello, this is Ryotsu speaking.

126
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:33,700
Ryo-chan, what on earth is going on here?

127
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:39,200
Did you two really swap bodies,
senpai and Reiko-san?

128
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:40,980
Looks like it.

129
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:41,300
Then -

130
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:43,280
Yes, I'm Reiko.

131
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:44,420
Really?

132
00:09:44,420 --> 00:09:45,620
It's true.

133
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:47,780
Really, really? Reiko?

134
00:09:47,780 --> 00:09:49,760
Really, really, it's me, Reiko.

135
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:54,920
Didn't you say, senpai,
that you swapped insides with me

136
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:56,980
and ran wild with my body?

137
00:09:57,780 --> 00:10:01,480
And yesterday you said you
wanted to swap with Reiko-san.

138
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:03,900
Are you saying I'm lying?

139
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:06,960
This is definitely Miss Reiko.

140
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:09,420
She knew things only
the young lady would know.

141
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:11,300
It was the same with me.

142
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:14,320
You're always thorough about
that sort of thing, senpai.

143
00:10:15,420 --> 00:10:16,400
This is hopeless.

144
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:20,620
As long as I'm in Ryo-chan's body,
no one will believe me.

145
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:27,240
Reiko-san

146
00:10:27,780 --> 00:10:28,240
Young lady!

147
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:28,900
Me!

148
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:31,600
Whoa! You've turned into washi paper,
and quite perfectly!

149
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:36,140
Honestly, Ryo-chan!
Don't go wandering around dressed like that!

150
00:10:36,220 --> 00:10:38,160
You're one to talk!

151
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:41,100
It really does look like we've swapped...

152
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:42,620
Are you convinced now?

153
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:47,460
No! With you, senpai,
it's never that simple...

154
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:51,460
Bravo! Bravo! Nobel Bravo! Pan!

155
00:10:52,920 --> 00:10:54,460
Enagigyaaagyuu!

156
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:58,980
Hmm it seems the experiment
was a great success after all.

157
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:02,940
Stop talking so carelessly
and change us back right now!

158
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:04,480
Apparently, that's impossible.

159
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:07,880
Why? Just use that machine again,
and we'll be fine!

160
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:12,480
N-no, that machine only swaps people.
It can't change them back.

161
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:17,580
What do you mean? So I'm stuck
like this for the rest of my life?

162
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:22,440
N-no, after half a day,
it's supposed to naturally return to normal.

163
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:23,400
Really?

164
00:11:24,460 --> 00:11:27,420
The words of the greatest scientist,
Korosuke Esaki, are never a lie!

165
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:29,160
That's a lie, you know!

166
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:32,040
Maybe they really did swap after all.

167
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:34,520
So you finally believe us?

168
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:37,240
No, there's some kind of trick to this...

169
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:41,320
Well, thanks to this,
we obtained valuable research data.

170
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:42,820
Then, Bitter Gen...

171
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:45,760
As irresponsible as ever.

172
00:11:45,760 --> 00:11:50,280
I have an appointment with
an important client today...

173
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:53,380
That's right! What should we do?

174
00:11:54,500 --> 00:12:04,580
With you looking like that, it's over. We can't cancel now.
I'll go in your place. I wonder if Ryo-chan will be all right.

175
00:12:05,260 --> 00:12:16,460
I suppose that's the best option in this case.
I'll play the part perfectly, so if you'd just let me handle it, it'll go smoothly.

176
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:24,220
Now, about the pay. Well, it's not like we're
getting any lessons beforehand, after all.

177
00:12:24,220 --> 00:12:32,220
This is sure to be a hit, you know. Ojou-sama...
Fine, I'll pay you if you do it properly.

178
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:40,500
Well then, Reiko, you're quick. So it's a deal.
Just sit back and leave it all to me, like you're on a big ship.

179
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:42,400
They really have swapped.

180
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:46,340
Are you ready?

181
00:12:46,340 --> 00:12:47,320
Okay.

182
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:48,460
Perfect.

183
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:51,040
Even if she is a rich young lady,

184
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:52,000
she's still a policewoman.

185
00:12:52,450 --> 00:12:54,020
Whatever you do, don't screw this up.

186
00:12:54,020 --> 00:12:55,060
Yes, sir.

187
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:03,740
The guest is a foreigner?

188
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:05,540
You didn't tell me, Reiko.

189
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:08,540
I can't speak a lick of English.

190
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:10,820
It's fine, Ryo-chan.

191
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:13,860
Mr. Smith is a big Japanophile,

192
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:16,500
and he speaks fluent Japanese,
so don't worry.

193
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:18,520
Geez, you scared me.

194
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:21,620
Anyway,
please make sure you don't offend him.

195
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:23,360
Leave it to me.

196
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:25,960
I'll play you to a T, so...

197
00:13:26,820 --> 00:13:28,720
I'm really worried.

198
00:13:29,300 --> 00:13:31,680
Ms. Reiko, sorry to keep you waiting.

199
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:34,100
Hello, hello, Mr. Smith.

200
00:13:34,100 --> 00:13:35,560
Long time no see.

201
00:13:38,180 --> 00:13:39,800
You're overdoing it, Ryo-chan.

202
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:42,920
I'm so happy to meet you.

203
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:46,160
Me too, Mr. Smith.

204
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:48,820
I look forward to working with you today.

205
00:13:48,820 --> 00:13:50,460
Got it, leave it to me.

206
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:51,740
Wait, that's not it.

207
00:13:52,140 --> 00:13:54,040
Leave it all to Reiko!

208
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:55,680
Come on, let's go.

209
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:59,140
Ryo-chan.

210
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:00,280
Sir.

211
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:05,180
Excuse me, are you meeting someone?

212
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:07,360
No, I'm...

213
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:11,880
But hey, just come over here for a moment.

214
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:21,520
Well then, Mr. Smith.
Reiko is best friends with Gyūbara Noriko.

215
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:24,680
Do you know her, Mr. Smith? Gyūbara Noriko?

216
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:30,900
Well, then you must also know Tetsu & Tomo's
"I wonder why" bit, of course.

217
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:34,980
Yes, of course.
Well then, the American crayfish...

218
00:14:34,980 --> 00:14:37,660
like the high-pitched tsukkomi
from when they did the voices.

219
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:39,560
No, that's a bit much.

220
00:14:39,940 --> 00:14:44,280
I see, I'll have to do my best.
American crayfish.

221
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:51,620
I had no idea you were a police officer.
I'm terribly sorry.

222
00:14:52,220 --> 00:14:54,480
It's just that you were
acting so suspiciously.

223
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:57,660
I suppose so. May I go now?

224
00:14:57,660 --> 00:14:58,140
Yes.

225
00:14:58,620 --> 00:14:59,260
Well then.

226
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:01,000
Excuse me.

227
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:21,420
Ryo-chan, can you hear me?

228
00:15:21,860 --> 00:15:23,480
Honestly, Sū-san is just...

229
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:24,620
Sū-san?

230
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:28,240
Wait, wait, Ryo-chan, what do you mean Sū-san?
What's with Sū-san?!

231
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:30,840
Shut up,
everything's going smoothly on this end.

232
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:32,700
What? Is something wrong?

233
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:34,760
No problem, no problem!

234
00:15:35,220 --> 00:15:36,400
Hey, Ryo-chan!

235
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:40,820
I told you to shut up, didn't I? Sū-san,
we're about to arrive at the destination.

236
00:15:40,820 --> 00:15:42,120
Hah...

237
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:52,680
How beautiful!

238
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:55,740
Reiko-san, I absolutely hate you!

239
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,200
Sū-san, you're such a smooth talker.

240
00:15:58,740 --> 00:16:01,140
I bet you say that to everyone.

241
00:16:06,320 --> 00:16:07,500
By the way, Ryo-chan.

242
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:09,680
You do know the tea
ceremony etiquette, right?

243
00:16:10,060 --> 00:16:12,520
How would I know something like that?

244
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:14,040
Then what are we going to do?

245
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,300
Don't worry about it.

246
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:16,840
The other party is a foreigner.

247
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:18,780
I don't know anything about etiquette.

248
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:20,600
That may be true, but...

249
00:16:52,620 --> 00:16:54,240
Eeeeeeh!

250
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:54,980
Mm.

251
00:16:54,980 --> 00:16:56,200
Mm.

252
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:56,800
Mm.

253
00:16:56,800 --> 00:17:03,140
Eeeeeeh!

254
00:17:03,140 --> 00:17:05,260
Aaaaaah!

255
00:17:05,260 --> 00:17:07,600
Aaaaaah!

256
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:39,480
Reiko-san, w-what's that?

257
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:41,140
Is something wrong?

258
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:44,353
The tea etiquette I know

259
00:17:44,403 --> 00:17:46,180
seems a little different.

260
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:47,045
Ahahaha,

261
00:17:47,095 --> 00:17:50,607
Mr. Smith may not be aware of this,

262
00:17:50,657 --> 00:17:53,231
but there are many schools of tea,

263
00:17:53,281 --> 00:17:54,980
and mine is the avant-garde school.

264
00:17:55,500 --> 00:17:56,480
Avant-garde school?

265
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:58,100
I hope that makes sense to you.

266
00:17:58,600 --> 00:18:00,100
Nice ice!

267
00:18:00,340 --> 00:18:01,520
T-together!

268
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:05,560
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

269
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:06,320
Right, haha.

270
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:08,520
Well, please.

271
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:09,200
Yes.

272
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:16,080
Is something the matter, Mr. Smith?

273
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,420
No, haha.

274
00:18:18,420 --> 00:18:21,200
I'm just not quite sure about
the tea ceremony etiquette...

275
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:24,400
Then allow me to show you how it's done.

276
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:26,320
Yes, like this...

277
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:35,920
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?
What was that scream?

278
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:39,720
Sū-san's just overjoyed
because the tea is so delicious.

279
00:18:42,460 --> 00:18:44,400
Sū-san, here's another cup.

280
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:46,400
Come on.

281
00:18:48,900 --> 00:18:50,880
Don't be shy about it.

282
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:53,300
Really now.

283
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:54,360
Don't hold back.

284
00:18:56,320 --> 00:18:56,660
Come on!

285
00:18:57,140 --> 00:18:58,560
Wait, wait, wait, really?

286
00:18:58,940 --> 00:19:01,300
Ryo-chan, what's wrong?
It's you, isn't it, Ryo-chan!

287
00:19:02,220 --> 00:19:04,100
Shut up, I'm fine!

288
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:07,060
Ryo-chan! Hey, Ryo-chan!

289
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:08,080
Come on!

290
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:30,100


291
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:36,140
Hello? Hello?

292
00:19:36,140 --> 00:19:36,860
What's wrong?

293
00:19:36,860 --> 00:19:40,000
There seems to have been
an incident in Room 9015.

294
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:44,440
Excuse me.

295
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:46,360
Is something the matter?

296
00:19:49,580 --> 00:19:51,320
What on earth happened?

297
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:56,100
Quick, contact Miss Reiko!

298
00:19:56,640 --> 00:19:57,660
What did you just say?

299
00:19:58,160 --> 00:20:00,320
That Mr. Smith is a fake?

300
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:04,120
He's posing as me and
trying to kidnap Miss Reiko.

301
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:06,140
Kidnap me?

302
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:08,820
No, no, not you, Miss Reiko.

303
00:20:09,680 --> 00:20:12,080
Yes, understood.
I'll let you know right away.

304
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:13,460
Ryo-chan.

305
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:20,320
Mr. Kiriyama.

306
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:24,680
What happened to Mr. Kiriyama?

307
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:27,600
He went home, saying he needed some rest.

308
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:28,960
I see.

309
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:33,880
According to the schedule, I'm pretty sure
the next thing is a kabuki performance.

310
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:35,460
Aren't we going the wrong way?

311
00:20:36,320 --> 00:20:37,920
The schedule has also been changed.

312
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:38,740
I see.

313
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:46,760
Target acquired.

314
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:50,120
Moving toward Okutama at
60 kilometers per hour.

315
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:50,360
Right.

316
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:57,040
Aaaaaah!

317
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:01,140
Come in.

318
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:06,900
Wh-what? Where is this?
Come on, come on, step inside.

319
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:08,940
Aaaaaah!

320
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:16,500
What on earth is going on? Reiko?

321
00:21:17,020 --> 00:21:18,900
Shh, keep it quiet.

322
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:24,460
Looks like they're
definitely inside, though.

323
00:21:24,460 --> 00:21:27,180
We can't tell what's happening,
so we can't make a move.

324
00:21:27,980 --> 00:21:31,000
But even if she's a hostage,
he is our senior, after all.

325
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:33,720
Well, I think she'll be fine.

326
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:36,040
What's wrong, Reiko-san?

327
00:22:00,220 --> 00:22:02,320
You're back to normal, Reiko.

328
00:22:02,320 --> 00:22:03,420
Thank goodness.

329
00:22:04,500 --> 00:22:06,080
So Ryo-chan must be back too.

330
00:22:09,140 --> 00:22:12,240
What is this, Sū-san? What's with the act?

331
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:16,100
Still don't get it?
You've given us nothing but trouble!

332
00:22:19,900 --> 00:22:44,000
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuughhh...

333
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:46,220
What happened to Mom, Sū-san?

334
00:22:47,640 --> 00:22:50,280
Senpai seems to be back to normal too.

335
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:51,620
Look.

336
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:54,700
What's wrong with you?

337
00:22:56,540 --> 00:22:57,060
Wait.

338
00:22:58,420 --> 00:23:01,100
Hey, help me.

339
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:04,580
Officer.

340
00:23:04,580 --> 00:23:05,540
Senpai.

341
00:23:05,540 --> 00:23:08,900
Reiko, you're back to normal?

342
00:23:08,900 --> 00:23:10,220
Ryo-chan, you too.

343
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:14,040
So Sū-san and the others were surprised.

344
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:16,680
That guy's a fake Mr. Smith.

345
00:23:17,100 --> 00:23:20,540
He was a kidnapper after Miss Reiko, Senpai.

346
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:21,860
What?

347
00:23:26,580 --> 00:23:27,600
So that's how it was.

348
00:23:28,180 --> 00:23:32,100
But kidnapping a senior officer...
those poor culprits.

349
00:23:32,100 --> 00:23:35,300
Yeah, but we swapped at a good time,
didn't we.

350
00:23:35,660 --> 00:23:37,660
We should thank Professor
Ezaki or something.

351
00:23:37,660 --> 00:23:40,780
By the way, Reiko, what about my fee?

352
00:23:41,120 --> 00:23:42,140
That's not happening.

353
00:23:42,280 --> 00:23:44,460
Mr. Smith was a fake, after all.

354
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:46,020
The contract is void.

355
00:23:46,160 --> 00:23:48,900
Aaaaaah, n-no way...

356
00:23:49,260 --> 00:23:51,840
All that effort for nothing, Senior.

357
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:55,220
Damn it, this is all that guy's fault.

358
00:23:55,980 --> 00:23:56,980
Ezaki!

359
00:23:59,940 --> 00:24:00,702
Well,

360
00:24:00,752 --> 00:24:04,000
From a certain point of view,
this experiment was a success.

361
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:04,080
Right!

362
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:36,480
Why do personalities change like that?

363
00:24:36,480 --> 00:24:38,060
The wealthy master of the realm.

364
00:24:38,060 --> 00:24:42,240
The guy who sleeps all day only
wakes up once every four years?

365
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:43,380
I wonder why.

366
00:24:43,380 --> 00:24:45,500
I wonder why.

367
00:24:46,260 --> 00:24:52,540
Nakagawa won't lend money to Ryo-san,

368
00:24:53,280 --> 00:24:56,280
but he'll lend out tanks and
fighter jets with no problem.

369
00:24:56,280 --> 00:24:59,580
I wonder why.

370
00:25:02,080 --> 00:25:06,920
Reiko is incredibly rich,

371
00:25:08,520 --> 00:25:12,460
so why does she work at the police box?

372
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:14,700
I wonder why.

373
00:25:14,700 --> 00:25:15,960
I wonder why.

374
00:25:16,520 --> 00:25:17,220
Why?

375
00:25:17,220 --> 00:25:17,920
Why?

376
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:18,600
Why?

377
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:19,540
I wonder why.

378
00:25:30,380 --> 00:25:33,960
What do you think? The Katsushika Police
Box Flying Squadron that I came up with,

379
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:36,280
is eco-friendly and makes no noise,

380
00:25:36,280 --> 00:25:38,300
and its patrol effectiveness is outstanding.

381
00:25:38,300 --> 00:25:41,780
You think I'm scheming some
kind of business or something?

382
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:43,980
As if I would ever do that!

383
00:25:43,980 --> 00:25:46,220
Next time: Fly! Flying Squadron!

384
00:25:46,220 --> 00:25:47,120
See you then.

385
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:50,680
That place has turtles.

386
00:25:51,880 --> 00:25:53,980
Well, surely there are turtles.

387
00:25:55,260 --> 00:25:59,160
Everyone, come visit our town!

388
00:26:00,120 --> 00:26:00,800
Thank you.

